-- risk: additive
--
-- #3132 (decided in #3012) -- an assistant proposes to invite a member, and
-- the person confirms in the app.
--
--   write  create_invitations  create_invitation, the invite step's own
--                              command (manageMembers), for a member, never
--                              an admin
--
-- The join code is NEVER returned: a code in an assistant's transcript is a
-- credential in a log. The answer names the invitation (its id) and its
-- status; whoever confirms reads the code in the app and passes it on. The
-- target (mcp_target_create_invitations) refuses before anyone is asked what
-- the command would refuse, names the invitee, and carries the count of open
-- invitations as its revision: a proposal made before another invitation
-- appeared is stale.

